 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing the acquisition of certain right-of-way easements, drainage easements, temporary construction easements, and property rights by negotiation or condemnation for use in public projects of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Nashville Department of Transportation and Multimodal Infrastructure (“NDOT”), for  the Cliff Drive Phase 1 Pedestrian Improvements, 30th Avenue North Pedestrian Improvements, and Harris Street Pedestrian Improvements, NDOT Project Number NDT 526.  (2026M-065AG-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, it is in the public interest that right-of-way easements, drainage easements, temporary construction easements, and property rights be acquired by the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, for use in a public project referenced herein as NDOT Project Number NDT 526, Proposal No. 2026M-065AG-001, the  sidewalk improvement projects on Cliff Drive from Buena Vista Pike to the mid-block of Cliff Drive, 30th Avenue North from Clare Avenue to Batavia Street, and Harris Street from Gallatin Pike to the mid-block of Harris Street, NDOT Project Number NDT 526, Proposal No. 2026M-065AG-001 (“the Project”); and,\nWHEREAS, the right-of-way easements, temporary construction easements and property rights associated with the Project are located on the properties described in Exhibits 1, 2, and 3, attached hereto and incorporated by reference; and, \nWHEREAS, the easements and property rights associated with the Project are further described in NDOT’s plans on file for the Project, which are incorporated by reference.\nNOW, THEREFORE BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.    \tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, by and through the Director of Public Property Administration, is hereby authorized to acquire, by negotiation or condemnation, right-of-way easements, drainage easements, temporary construction easements,  and property rights for use in public projects of the Metropolitan Government, acting by and through the Nashville Department of Transportation and Multimodal Infrastructure (NDOT), initially for  Cliff Drive Phase 1 Pedestrian Improvements, 30th Avenue North Phase 1 Pedestrian Improvements, and Harris Street Phase 1 Pedestrian Improvements, NDOT Project No. NDT 526, Proposal No. 2026M-065AG-001 (“the Project”), the same being for a public purpose and the public convenience requiring it. \nSection 2.    The easements and property rights to be acquired for the Project are located on the properties described in Exhibits 1, 2, and 3, attached hereto and incorporated by reference herein, and described in NDOT’s plans on file for the Project, which are incorporated by reference herein.\nSection 3.    \tThe Director of Public Property Administration is hereby authorized and directed, to acquire by negotiation or, if necessary, to take and appropriate by condemnation proceedings the interests in real property described herein in the name of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County for use in the public project referenced herein.\nSection 4.    \tAll necessary and incidental costs of the right-of-way easements and property rights herein authorized to be acquired shall be paid from funds authorized from Business Unit No. 42406826.\nSection 5.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution. \nSection 6.    \tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n\n\n"
